<title>CANADA: Petro-Canada cuts posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Petro-Canada cuts posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petro-Canada said it lowered the price it would pay for some grades of crude oil by C$8.00/cubic meter or C$1.27/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The new prices were listed as follows: Edmonton light sweet C$165.00/cubic meter, or C$26.23/barrel Cromer light sour C$158.00/cubic meter, or C$25.12/barrel Hardisty medium C$126.00/cubic meter, or C$20.03/barrel ((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
